accounts-empty-title = An account can sign in without a password
accounts-empty-summary = The account { $user } has an empty password and a real shell.
accounts-uid0-title = Another account has administrator rights
accounts-uid0-summary = The account { $user } has user id 0, the same power as root.
accounts-lockout-title = Repeated wrong passwords are not slowed down
accounts-lockout-summary = No account lockout (faillock) is configured, so a password can be guessed without limit.
accounts-password_max_age-title = Passwords never expire
accounts-password_max_age-summary = No maximum password age is set, so a password is valid forever.
accounts-inactive-title = Inactive accounts are not locked
accounts-inactive-summary = The inactive-account default is "never", so dormant accounts stay usable.
accounts-file_perms-title = A sensitive file has the wrong permissions
accounts-file_perms-summary = { $file } should be owned by root with its default mode.
accounts-sudo_logging-title = sudo does not record what it runs
accounts-sudo_logging-summary = No sudo logging (log_input, log_output or logfile) is configured.
accounts-login_banner-title = No login banner is shown
accounts-login_banner-summary = Neither /etc/issue nor an sshd banner is set.
